A forearm link for a humanoid robot arm, as an engineer would first draw it. One solid body. The joint axes run along Y.

- Elbow end: a disc Ã˜70, Y -4 to 4, centred on the origin, axis along Y. It bolts to a motor's output through six
  Ã˜3.4 holes on a Ã˜50 circle (the first on +X in the X-Z plane, 60 degrees apart), with a Ã˜30 locating bore through it.
- Beam: a box X -20 to 20, Y -15 to 15, running from Z -32 to Z -170. It runs into the rim of the disc.
- Wrist end: a fork. Two cheeks, each X -15 to 15, Z -170 to -215, one at Y 16 to 22 and one at Y -22 to -16, joined to
  the beam by a block X -20 to 20, Y -22 to 22, Z -170 to -180. A Ã˜8 pin hole through both cheeks along Y at X 0,
  Z -200.

